Third-party components
===============================================================================

1. homr (Optical Music Recognition engine)
   https://github.com/liebharc/homr
   License: GNU AGPL-3.0 (repository LICENSE)
   Packages/omr-homr-ios is a Swift port of homr at commit
   7d97c3cee4ad772b50266fdf9dc78bbf9064701e (page preprocessing, SegNet
   tiling, staff detection, dewarping, tokenizers/vocabulary, decode loop).
   The bundled tokenizer and vocabulary JSON files are copied or exported from
   homr/transformer/. homr credits the two projects below.

2. oemer
   https://github.com/BreezeWhite/oemer
   License: MIT (repository LICENSE; its copyright line is the unfilled
   template "Copyright (c) [year] [fullname]"; project author: BreezeWhite)
   homr's UNet segmentation models are adapted from oemer. No oemer source
   code is included in this app.

3. Polyphonic-TrOMR
   https://github.com/NetEase/Polyphonic-TrOMR
   License: Apache License 2.0 (repository LICENSE; text in Appendix A)
   homr's transformer staff-recognition model is based on Polyphonic-TrOMR.
   No Polyphonic-TrOMR source code is included in this app.

4. homr ONNX model weights
   https://github.com/liebharc/homr/releases/tag/onnx_checkpoints
   Files (pinned by SHA-256 in models.lock, fetched by scripts/fetch-models,
   not committed to git, bundled in the app):
     segnet_308-3296ccd40960f90ca6ab9c035cca945675d30a0f_fp16.onnx
     encoder_pytorch_model_465-597144cab54c8f6d0f6c9619df5c5312694eadd6_fp16.onnx
     decoder_pytorch_model_465-597144cab54c8f6d0f6c9619df5c5312694eadd6.onnx
   License: the release notes ("Pretrained onnx models for homr") and the
   homr README state no separate license for the weights. They are
   distributed by the homr project in its GitHub releases, so they are treated
   here as covered by the homr repository license, GNU AGPL-3.0. They are used
   unmodified.

